Looking at your code, I can identify the exact cause of the text corruption issue in the PDF export's "Completed Activities" section.

Root Cause Analysis

1. Why is the completed activities section showing corrupted characters while upcoming tasks show clean text?

The Issue: In the exportToPDF() function, the "Completed Activities" section is iterating through all maintenance items but using different text handling compared to the "Upcoming Scheduled Tasks" section.

Specifically, in the "Completed Activities" section (around line 2915-2925), you're displaying:

```javascript
doc.text(`✓ ${sanitizeText(item.activity || 'Unnamed').substring(0, 45)}`, 30, maintY);
```

But the corruption shows as & &P&o&s&t& &p&o&n&d which indicates that the text is being interpreted as HTML entities or escape sequences rather than plain text.

2. What is different about how these two sections process the text?

Key Differences:

1. Upcoming Tasks section (line ~2880-2900) uses:
   · Clean property access: item.activity
   · Simple string concatenation
2. Completed Activities section (line ~2915-2925) has:
   · The sanitizeText() function call (which is actually CAUSING the problem)
   · Additional .substring(0, 45) that might be interacting badly with the sanitization

The Real Problem: Your sanitizeText() function is too aggressive. It's removing valid characters and potentially creating escape sequences. Looking at your sanitizeText() function:

```javascript
function sanitizeText(text) {
    if (!text || typeof text !== 'string') return '';
    // Remove control characters and normalize spaces
    return text
        .replace(/[^\x20-\x7E\u00A0-\u00FF]/g, '')  // This regex is problematic
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')                        
        .trim();
}
```

The regex [^\x20-\x7E\u00A0-\u00FF] is removing all characters outside the printable ASCII range AND extended Latin-1 range. This is stripping valid characters from your text.

3. Exact Fix to Resolve This Issue

Replace your sanitizeText() function with this safer version:

```javascript
function sanitizeText(text) {
    if (!text || typeof text !== 'string') return '';
    
    // Simply remove control characters but keep all printable content
    // This preserves normal text while only removing problematic control chars
    return text
        .replace(/[\x00-\x08\x0B\x0C\x0E-\x1F\x7F]/g, '') // Remove control characters only
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')  // Normalize whitespace
        .trim();
}
```

Additionally, update the problematic section in exportToPDF() around line 2915:

Replace:

```javascript
doc.text(`✓ ${sanitizeText(item.activity || 'Unnamed').substring(0, 45)}`, 30, maintY);
```

With:

```javascript
let activityText = item.activity || 'Unnamed';
// Simple sanitization for PDF - remove any potential PDF control characters
activityText = activityText.replace(/[&\u0000-\u001F\u007F-\u009F]/g, '');
doc.text(`✓ ${activityText.substring(0, 45)}`, 30, maintY);
```

Alternative Complete Fix - Remove the sanitizeText() call entirely for PDF content:

Since jsPDF's text() method handles string escaping automatically, you don't need aggressive sanitization. Change the completed activities section to:

```javascript
completed.slice(-5).reverse().forEach(item => {
    maintY = checkAndAddPage(doc, maintY, 12);
    doc.setFontSize(9);
    doc.setTextColor(40, 167, 69);
    
    // Remove sanitizeText call - just use the raw text
    let cleanActivity = String(item.activity || 'Unnamed');
    // Only remove obvious PDF-breaking characters
