    doc.text(`✓ ${cleanActivity.substring(0, 45)}`, 30, maintY);
    maintY += 5;
    doc.setFontSize(8);
    doc.setTextColor(100, 100, 100);
    doc.text(`  Completed: ${formatDateStr(item.date)}`, 32, maintY);
    maintY += 8;
});
```

Summary

The corruption occurs because:

1. Your sanitizeText() function uses an overly broad regex that strips valid characters
2. The ampersand (&) characters in your text are being misinterpreted as PDF escape sequences
3. The completed activities section uses this function while upcoming tasks don't

Apply the fix by:

1. Replacing the sanitizeText() function with the safer version above
2. Or better yet, remove the sanitizeText() call from the PDF generation code entirely
3. Use simple string replacement to remove only known problematic characters

This will resolve the & &P&o&s&t& &p&o&n&d corruption issue while maintaining proper text rendering in your PDF exports.
